====Usage notes====
* The plural {{m|en|virii}}, though common, is based on a misunderstanding of Latin. In classical Latin, {{m|la|virus}} appears to be a [[singulare tantum]] without any attested plural. If {{m|la|virus}} were a masculine 2nd declension noun, it would form its plural with a singular ''-i'' as {{m|en|viri}}. In fact as a neuter 2nd declension noun, in New Latin, the plural is formed as {{m|en|vira}}.

